windowDescribeT -- windows stroke B (2026-11-23, SEQ 758): describe on select. Tester's shape.
Selecting a field puts its description (dESCRIPTIONs' entry of the field's name) in the form's help box, the first
field carrying a describe attribute. Read from the floor's own trace: how many characters the help box drew, of how many.
WD-0  nothing selected: each help box shows its own text (firstLight's 61 characters, wdForm's 8).
WD-1  firstLight's heading: the box holds describeHead's 2008 characters and draws what fits.
WD-2  a picture: saber's 111.   WD-3  the help box itself: nothing changes, still saber's 111.
WD-4  wdForm's A: its 49.       WD-5  the help box itself: still A's 49.
WD-6  B, which has no description: the box is back to its own 8 -- so no layout ever wrote the definition.
WD-7  a form with no help box: the click selects and nothing else happens; no describe line, nothing refused.
